{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>They did.</b> The reason for \"they did\" regarding Moses is because he spoke to Aaron that he should strike with the staff, as is the way: \"and your staff with which you struck the river\" (Exodus 17:5)." "<b>And it was the lice.</b> A species name, and the mem is added, or it is in place of the heh and is not a root letter; and sometimes it is a feminine marker, like צפרדעים, for a single one, \"and the frog came up\" (Exodus 7:28 [sic]). And the proof is כנים, and the word הכנם is strange because of the addition of the mem, like ריקם, חנם, and יפת אמר, for the mem is a marker, for a single one, thus from כנים like פת מפתים, and this is the word in the manner of בתוך האהלי (Joshua 7:21). And do not wonder because it says \"all the dust of the earth was lice,\" because he struck with the staff in one place, for so it was with the matter of the waters and the matter of the boils — for the meaning is that then the plague began."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {1 "Verse cited as למעלה פ' ב (Exodus 7:28) corresponds to the frog plague; the chapter/verse numbering follows the Hebrew text as Ibn Ezra gives it."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:40.819084328Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}